<worksheet>
  <title>Quiz: Describing Numerical Data Attempt 1</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Name: <fillin characters="45"/>
    </p>

    <assemblage>
      <p>
        <ul cols="2">
          <li><p><c>mean(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>median(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>sd(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>var(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>sd(x)*sqrt((n-1)/n)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>min(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>max(x)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>quantile(x, type = 2)</c></p></li>
          <li><p><c>IQR(x, type = 2)</c></p></li>
          <li><p>Lower outlier fence: Q1 - 1.5 * IQR</p></li>
          <li><p>Upper outlier fence: Q3 + 1.5 * IQR</p></li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </assemblage>
  </introduction>
  <page>
  <exercise workspace=".5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Data was collected for a sample of organic snacks. The amount of sugar (in mg) in each snack is summarized in the histogram below.
      </p>
      <p>
        <image source="images/sugar-histogram.png" width="35%">
          <description>
            Histogram of sugar amounts in milligrams. The intervals from
            220 to 360 milligrams have width 20 milligrams and frequencies
            4, 4, 10, 14, 8, 4, and 2, respectively.
          </description>
        </image>
      </p>
      <p>How would you best describe the meaning of the fourth bin (or class>?</p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise workspace="0.5in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the mean, median, and standard deviation of the following data sample.
      </p>
      <p>
        <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="center" valign="middle"
         top="medium" left="medium" bottom="medium" right="medium">
          <row>
            <cell right="medium"><m>x</m></cell>
            <cell>49.8</cell>
            <cell>37.4</cell>
            <cell>24</cell>
            <cell>43.9</cell>
            <cell>16</cell>
            <cell>22.1</cell>
            <cell>26.3</cell>
            <cell>45</cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </p>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
</page>
<page>
  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        The histogram below shows the ages (in years) of Honda Civic automobiles listed for sale on the Seattle Times Web site on November 26, 2003.
      </p>
      <p>
        <image source="images/car-age-histogram.png" width="25%">
          <description>
            Histogram of car ages in years. The intervals from 2 to 18
            years have width 2 years and frequencies 4, 16, 15, 9, 8,
            4, 5, and 2, respectively.
          </description>
        </image>
      </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.1in">
        <p>What is the shape of the histogram?</p>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.1in">
        <p>Which measure fo center is most appropriate for this data?</p>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.1in">
        <p>Which is larger for this data, the mean, the median or are they approximately the same?</p>
      </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        A box-and-whisker plot for the sample data set <q>My Data</q> is shown, along with additional statistics.
      </p>

      <image source="images/my-data-boxplot.png" width="40%">
        <description>
          Horizontal box plot with minimum 20, first quartile 45,
          median 55, third quartile 70, and maximum 77.
        </description>
      </image>

      <p>
        <me>\bar{x}=54.8 \qquad s=16.1 \qquad n=81</me>
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>Find each of the following.</p>
        <ul cols="3">
          <li><p>Range: </p></li>
          <li><p>Median: </p></li>
          <li><p>Interquartile range:</p></li>
        </ul>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Approximately what proportion of the data falls between
          <m>45</m> and <m>77</m>? Give your answer as a decimal
          rounded to two decimal places.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          Does the box plot suggest that the data are skewed left,
          skewed right, or approximately symmetric?
          Explain how you know.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>
